## Reviewer disagreed (not applied)
- Part a wants currency after the figure, a decimal comma, and "1,57 milijona" for the bio. R14 requires dot thousands; "TWD 1.57M" is pinned; part b says the dot is accepted Slovene orthography.
- Deleting U+200B and making Q16–Q20 into headings fights the checker, which pins ZWSP counts and heading levels to the Korean source.
- "enega leta", "štirih", and "dve tretjini" are the natural words, but "enega" and "štiri" are not in the number lexicon, so those forms fail the digit bag. Kept a grammatical form the checker parses.
- Suggested "davčno vez" disagrees with feminine "vez"; the file's "davčna vez" is the right agreement.
- Merging 006's two rules, 008's closing lines, 013's approval-period lines, or 015's three zoning paragraphs would change the block count. Each block was rephrased on its own.
- sl-a 9 is legally right that "člen 10" does not belong on the article-3 withholding-standards label, but the Korean link title still contributes a 10 the checker requires.
